---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 2 -- ENABLE THE IPv4 TELNET SERVER
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Designed expectation: `service telnet ip` is accepted, `show telnet` reads Enabled / IPv4 /
23, and the configuration appears in the running-config.

Sent (11:45:15, first attempt, work/t1-on.log) -- VERBATIM, with the device prompts:

    awplus# configure terminal
    Enter configuration commands, one per line.  End with CNTL/Z.
    awplus(config)# service telnet ip
    % Warning: Telnet is insecure and deprecated. Please use SSH.
    awplus(config)#

`cfg.py` exited 2 on that `% ` line ("!!! CLI error on 'service telnet ip' -- stopping") and
abandoned the rest of the batch.  THAT IS THE DRIVER, NOT THE PRODUCT: the prompt advanced
and the command took effect.  Proof, read immediately afterwards (11:45:39, work/t1-verify.log;
the console was left clean at `awplus#`, checked with peek):

    awplus# show telnet
    Telnet Server Configuration
    ------------------------------------------------------------
    Telnet server                      : Enabled
    Protocol                           : IPv4
    Port                               : 23
    awplus# show running-config | include telnet
    service telnet
    no service telnet ipv6

MEASURED PRODUCT FACT worth recording: the IPv4-only form is stored in the running-config as
the generic `service telnet` PLUS an explicit `no service telnet ipv6`.  It is not stored as
`service telnet ip`.  With both protocols on, the running-config carries only `service telnet`
(see STEP 4).  So the running-config distinguishes the three states by which negation is
present, and a `| include telnet` grep must be read with that in mind.

`tools/console.py` ADVISORY was then extended with `Telnet is insecure and deprecated` and
the same batch re-ran cleanly in STEP 4 (`(advisory, not an error -- continuing)`).

The DUT logged the warning itself, which is the product's own record of the same event:
    2026 Oct 19 22:45:02 user.warning awplus IMI[903]: Warning: Telnet is insecure and
    deprecated. Please use SSH.
STEP 2 VERDICT: PASS.

