STEP 6 -- REMOVAL: `no service telnet` and the refusal returns
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Designed expectation (memory `satisfactory-level-of-testing`: the step text is the floor,
always also prove removal): the feature disappears from `show telnet` and from the
running-config, and the identical connection attempt is refused again.

Capture armed: tools/tb capture tb277 ckmgmt eth3 40 t33378-removed.pcap tcp port 23

Sent (11:49:0x, work/t7-removed.log):

    awplus# configure terminal
    awplus(config)# no service telnet
    awplus(config)# end
    awplus# show telnet
    Telnet Server Configuration
    ------------------------------------------------------------
    Telnet server                      : Disabled
    Protocol                           : None
    Port                               : 23
    awplus# show running-config | include telnet
    no service telnet

Identical to the baseline read in STEP 1, including the disappearance of the
`no service telnet ipv6` line that the IPv4-only state had added.

    tools/tb tool tb277 ckmgmt netlogin --proto telnet --host 10.38.22.34 --user manager
        --password friend --login-timeout 10
      -> TRANSPORT FAILED: telnet 10.38.22.34:23 -- [Errno 111] Connection refused  (exit 4)

    file /tmp/ckmgmt/t33378-removed.pcap: 2 packet(s) total, 1 TCP flow(s) on port 23
    flow 10.38.22.33:57720 <-> 10.38.22.34:23  packets=2  duration=0.000s
         => REFUSED (SYN answered by RST)
       10.38.22.33:57720 -> 10.38.22.34:23  pkts=1  payload=0 B  flags={SYN}
       10.38.22.34:23 -> 10.38.22.33:57720  pkts=1  payload=0 B  flags={RST.ACK}

Two packets in the whole 40 s window: the same instrument that recorded 94 packets while the
