NOT MEASURED, AND SAID PLAINLY
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* REBOOT PERSISTENCE IS NOT MEASURED, for this case and for the whole group.  The DUT's
  underlay (vlan10/vlan48 and the access ports that carry them) exists in the RUNNING
  configuration only; the boot config is `flash:/default.cfg`.  A reload would destroy the
  very path every case in this campaign measures through, and writing the underlay to
  startup-config is a bench change (STANDING-ORDERS §4) that is not made unattended.  So
  this case does NOT show that `service telnet ip` survives a reboot.  Same statement as
  groups A and B.  This is a declared gap, not an omission.
* The IPv6 telnet listener was never connected to (no IPv6 address on the DUT's SVIs).
* `line vty 0 7` was left at its default; the number of simultaneous telnet sessions
  (TPS row 1295's subject) was not exercised -- one session at a time was used.

